  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> &nbsp;be any natural number&nbsp;</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>99</mn></math>&nbsp;are values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;or observation.</p><p>Now mean of the observation is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>x</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>99</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>x</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>99</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>x</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>x</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>99</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Mean deviation about mean<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></msubsup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">x</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>99</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>97</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>95</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>99</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>50</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>99</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p>So, it is true for every natural no. &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> &#39; as there is no term of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in mean deviation.</p>"
